findings.problem:
The outcome out-parameter, the diagnostic counters and the wait-bound and fault macros exist only under BPFTIME_DEVHASH_TEST. The out-parameter changes the insert's signature. So S3.1-S3.4 (C5's runs, run d and the controls) all run devhash_test_ptx.h.

The shipped devhash_ptx.h runs on the GPU only in:
- S3.9 (return codes);
- the S6 GPU test (pointers and return codes);
- S5.6, S5.7 and S8 (aggregate sums).

None of these applies the RULES-round2 checks that need no outcome channel:
- no key in two slots;
- count = live + refused;
- live = min(keys, max_entries);
- E2BIG = 0 when keys <= max_entries;
- no slot left claiming.

A difference confined to the macro-guarded code would go unseen. The plan also does not say which build S3.1 runs.

These tests name neither a mutation nor '(no mutation: reason)':
- S5.4 (takeover after a clean exit);
- the S6 mirrors of the 1531 cases (:76, :135, :171/:242, :185, :223, :289, :514, :642, key forwarding);
- S6 'the text is inserted once and before every function, and not at all when unused' (the ptxas mutation covers only 'before');
- S6 'by-value is kept beside lat's 1530 lookups';
- the S8 rules.

verdicts.reason:
