findings.problem:
No mutation and no reason are given for:
- S5.4 (takeover after a clean exit);
- S3.2 (run d seeded; S3.3's mutation is listed under S3.3 only);
- S3.11's third check (trampoline_ptx.h is sm_61-legal);
- the nine S6 mirrors of test_sum_map_routing.cpp;
- S6's 'inserted once and before every function, and not at all when unused';
- S6's 'by-value is kept beside lat's 1530 lookups'.
S2.11's no-mutation reason covers only the acquire load. 'In phase 1 lookups come from the table' is observable, so it can have a mutation. S3.3's mutation 'count not copied' changes the S3 harness, because S5's get_gpu_mem_buffer copy does not exist yet. It therefore does not exercise takeover_image().
